problem:
Problem description
- There is a set of candidate commercial properties $$\mathcal{P}$$ indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$, considered over a single investment horizon $$H$$.
- Each property $$p$$ has an annual income parameter $$r_p$$, an acquisition cost parameter $$c_p$$, and an availability parameter $$u_p$$.
- The decision is to select a subset of the available properties for purchase, with each property either purchased or not purchased.
- The total acquisition cost of the selected properties must stay within the available budget $$B$$.
- Any properties listed as incompatible in the set $$\mathcal{I}$$ cannot be purchased together in the same portfolio.
- The objective is to maximize the total annual income generated by the selected portfolio over the planning horizon.
- A solution is represented by:
  - A binary selection variable $$x_p$$ for each property $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$, where $$x_p = 1$$ means property $$p$$ is purchased and $$x_p = 0$$ means it is not purchased.
  - The chosen portfolio, which is the set of properties whose corresponding selection variable equals $$1$$.

Input Format
{
  "H": {
    "symbol": "$$H$$",
    "meaning": "number of planning periods in the evaluation horizon"
  },
  "P": {
    "symbol": "$$P$$",
    "meaning": "number of candidate properties"
  },
  "r": {
    "symbol": "$$r_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$P$$]",
    "meaning": "annual income generated by property $$p$$"
  },
  "c": {
    "symbol": "$$c_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$P$$]",
    "meaning": "acquisition cost of property $$p$$"
  },
  "u": {
    "symbol": "$$u_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$P$$]",
    "meaning": "available units of property $$p$$"
  },
  "B": {
    "symbol": "$$B$$",
    "meaning": "maximum total acquisition budget"
  },
  "I": {
    "symbol": "$$\mathcal{I}$$",
    "shape": "[$$K$$, $$2$$]",
    "meaning": "list of incompatible property pairs $$\left(p,q\right)$$ that cannot both be selected"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "x": {
    "symbol": "$$x$$",
    "shape": "[$$P$$]",
    "meaning": "binary purchase decision vector, where the $$p$$-th entry indicates whether property $$p$$ is selected"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "H": 1,
  "P": 4,
  "r": [12500, 35000, 23000, 100000],
  "c": [1500000, 2100000, 2300000, 4200000],
  "u": [1, 1, 1, 1],
  "B": 7000000,
  "I": [[4, 3]]
}
